[WORK]
UID: WORK-GRAMMAR-TAB-GROUPS
TITLE: Group the Grammars tab for reasoning, guarded by a coverage check
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Group the Grammars tab by a hand-authored layout file, grammar-groups.json,
that places the grammar's node types into sections and groups for reasoning.
Section Spec holds group Definition, drawn as a 2x2 grid of the definition
family on the two axes DEC-NODE-FAMILIES rules (normative vs descriptive,
all vs one: REQUIREMENT normative/all, DECISION normative/one, MECHANISM
descriptive/all, EVIDENCE descriptive/one), and group Coverage, holding
USE_CASE. Section Unsorted holds every remaining type until the operator
organizes them; its purpose is to surface the grammar-file splits they may
want (WORK-GRAMMAR-FILE-SPLIT). Two guards make the hand-authored file an
allowed exception to REQ-BOARD-GRAMMAR-DRIVEN rather than a violation: a
static check in nix flake check that every grammar node type is placed
exactly once or falls into the one catch-all, and that no placed type is
stale; and a runtime check on the page that shows a loud red banner for a
missing or stale type and never hides a type. Visually, each section is a
top-level heading followed by a horizontal rule, each group a subtitle, and
under it the cards centered or the 2x2 grid as a custom widget. The
Perspective pill moves to the end of the view switcher.
<<<
